  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Dutch contribution to the DESA Financing for Development Trust Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">General Assembly resolution 78/231 has &#x201C;urged those countries able to, and other potential donors, to contribute generously to the Trust Fund for the Follow-up to the International Conference on Financing for Development (FfD4), to facilitate a strengthened and more effective and inclusive intergovernmental process for carrying out the financing for development follow-up&#x201D;. Given the Netherlands&apos; desire to make FfD4 an inclusive process, the Directorate-General for International Cooperation (DGIS)of the MFA has decided to allocate EUR100.000 to this fund from The MFA fund for general ODA activities (Algemene ODA Activiteiten &#x2013; AOA) budget. Contributions will be used to: i) support the participation of developing countries and countries in special situations at the preparatory committee sessions and the Conference; ii) support stakeholder participation from the global South; and iii) support participation of experts, academics and think tanks to ensure the latest analysis and thinking is available to support the work of Member States.</narrative>
  </description>
